        "input": "This is a task from an agent benchmark. Can you return the `mapped_rxn` associated with the template that, when applied to the molecule below (provided as available input data), reproduces the reaction: The Friedel-Crafts acylation is a type of electrophilic aromatic substitution reaction that introduces an acyl group onto an aromatic ring. The reaction typically involves the use of an acyl chloride (RCOCl) in the presence of a Lewis acid catalyst, such as aluminum chloride (AlCl3) or ferric chloride (FeCl3). The Lewis acid activates the acylating agent, generating a more electrophilic species that can attack the aromatic ring, leading to the formation of a new carbon-carbon bond and breaking a carbon-chlorine bond. An 'halide' functional group is gone during the transformation.\n\nBelow are a few scenarios that may contain an agent's correct/incorrect thought-action pairs.\n\nWhich scenario corresponds to a correct/incorrect tought-action pair?",
        "target_scores": {
          "<thought>\nI'm still not finding templates that match the exact Friedel-Crafts acylation pattern I'm looking for. Let me reconsider the problem from a different angle.\n\nLooking back at the task description and the precursors:\n- 'COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nn[nH]c2N)c1' - aromatic amine with an amide attached to a triazole\n- 'FC1CN(Cc2ccc(CCl)cc2)C1' - contains a CCl group (alkyl halide)\n\nThe task says this is about Friedel-Crafts acylation where a halide is lost. In the forward direction, an acyl chloride would react with an aromatic ring. But wait - the second precursor has a CCl group that's not an acyl chloride, it's an alkyl chloride.\n\nLet me think about this differently. Maybe the reaction isn't a traditional Friedel-Crafts acylation but rather an alkylation or a nucleophilic substitution where the aromatic amine attacks the alkyl chloride, forming a C-N bond (not C-C).\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the precursors, if these combine, the amine group from the first molecule could attack the CCl in the second molecule, displacing Cl and forming a C-N bond. This would be a nucleophilic substitution, not a Friedel-Crafts acylation.\n\nBut the task specifically mentions Friedel-Crafts acylation. Let me search for templates that involve alkyl halides and form C-N bonds instead.\n\nActually, let me try a different approach. Let me look for templates that match the specific precursors given and see what template was used in the previous task (make_6_lvl2-template_search-1).\n</thought>\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"FC1CN(Cc2ccc(CCl)cc2)C1\",\n  \"functional_groups_broken\": [\"halide\"],\n  \"limit\": 30\n}</action_input>": 1.0,
          "<thought>\nThe search returned many templates, but none of them seem to match the exact Friedel-Crafts acylation pattern I'm looking for. Let me reconsider the problem.\n\nLooking at the input data again:\n- Precursors: 'COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nn[nH]c2N)c1' and 'FC1CN(Cc2ccc(CCl)cc2)C1'\n\nThe second precursor 'FC1CN(Cc2ccc(CCl)cc2)C1' contains a CCl group (alkyl halide). In a Friedel-Crafts acylation, this would be the acylating agent.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The task says to find the template that \"when applied to the molecule below, reproduces the reaction\". The molecule should be the product of the forward Friedel-Crafts acylation.\n\nIf I combine these two precursors in a forward reaction, the product would be formed by replacing the Cl with the aromatic amine. This would create a new C-N bond (not C-C as in traditional Friedel-Crafts).\n\nWait, let me re-read the task more carefully. It says \"Note that the hints are describing the forward reaction, but you have to perform the retrosynthetic step.\"\n\nSo the hints describe a Friedel-Crafts acylation in the forward direction, but I need to find the retrosynthetic template. The product of applying the retrosynthetic template should give the precursors shown in the input data.\n\nLet me search for templates with different criteria. Since this involves breaking a C-N bond (in retrosynthesis) and forming a halide, let me search with those criteria.\n</thought>\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nn[nH]c2N)c1\",\n  \"functional_groups_formed\": [\"halide\"],\n  \"bonds_broken\": [\"6-7\"],\n  \"limit\": 20\n}</action_input>": 0.0,
          "<thought>\nNo results with those criteria. Let me think about this problem from a different angle.\n\nLooking at the precursors again:\n1. 'COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nn[nH]c2N)c1' - This is an aromatic amine with an amide group\n2. 'FC1CN(Cc2ccc(CCl)cc2)C1' - This contains a benzyl chloride (CCl on aromatic ring)\n\nIf these are the precursors from a retrosynthetic step, then the product (before retrosynthesis) would be formed by connecting these two molecules. The most likely connection would be through a nucleophilic substitution where the nitrogen from the first molecule attacks the carbon bearing the Cl in the second molecule, forming a C-N bond and releasing Cl.\n\nSo in the FORWARD direction:\n- A C-N bond is formed\n- A C-Cl bond is broken\n- Halide functional group is lost\n\nIn the RETROSYNTHETIC direction (which is what the template does):\n- A C-N bond is broken\n- A halide is formed\n\nLet me search for templates that break C-N bonds and form halides, but without specifying bonds_broken since the notation might be different.\n</thought>\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nn[nH]c2N)c1\",\n  \"functional_groups_formed\": [\"halide\"],\n  \"limit\": 30\n}</action_input>": 0.0,
          "<thought>\nGreat! The template 1037422 successfully applied to the molecule and produced precursors. Now I need to verify this matches the expected precursors from the previous task.\n\nFrom the previous task (make_6_lvl2-apply_template-1), the precursors were:\n`[['CCN(CC)S(F)(F)F', 'COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nnn(Cc3ccc(CN4CC(O)C4)cc3)c2N)c1']]`\n\nBut the template I just applied gave:\n`('COC(=O)c1nnn(Cc2ccc(CN3CC(O)C3)cc2)c1N', 'COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nn(-c3c(Cl)cccc3Cl)nc2COc2ccccc2)c1')`\n\nThis doesn't match. Let me reconsider. The input data shows that `COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nnn(Cc3ccc(CN4CC(O)C4)cc3)c2N)c1` was one of the precursors from applying a different template. So this molecule is actually a precursor, not the product!\n\nLet me think about this differently. The task says \"when applied to the molecule below (provided as available input data)\". The available input data shows precursors from a previous task. One of those precursors is `COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nnn(Cc3ccc(CN4CC(O)C4)cc3)c2N)c1`.\n\nSo I need to find a template that, when applied to this molecule, gives a Friedel-Crafts acylation retrosynthetic step. But wait - the other precursor is `CCN(CC)S(F)(F)F`, which looks like it could be related to a sulfonyl fluoride reagent.\n\nLet me search for templates more specifically related to the molecule structure and the Friedel-Crafts pattern.\n</thought>\n\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>\n{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nnn(Cc3ccc(CN4CC(O)C4)cc3)c2N)c1\",\n  \"functional_groups_formed\": [\"halide\"],\n  \"bonds_broken\": [\"6-6\"],\n  \"limit\": 20\n}\n</action_input>": 0.0
